    "ls|LS16_S9_U_108": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 108 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.07.2016 \n \nOnline Content \n*108.  SHRI HARI OM PANDAY: \n           SHRI DHARMENDRA YADAV: \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Ministry has signed any  Memorandum of Understanding with non-\nGovernmental bodies for providing \"Digital/Online Content\" throughout the day and free of \ncost for the benefit of students and if so, the details and the salient features thereof; \n \n(b) whether the Ministry proposes to launch Massive Open Online Courses (MOOC) \nplatform 'Swayam' to provide high quality education on various subjects covering all \ndisciplines and also dedicated 'Prashikshak', a teacher education portal in the country and \nif so, the details and the salient features thereof; \n \n(c) the time by which the said facilities are likely to be launched; and \n \n(d) the manner and extent to which MOOC would be beneficial for th e education system \nas well as to the students? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \nPart (a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the table of the House. \n*** \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO  PARTS (a) TO (d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 108 ASKED BY  SHRI HARI OM  PANDAY AND  \nSHRI DHARMENDRA YADAV REGARDING ONLINE CONTENT \n \n(a) No Madam, Ministry has not signed Me morandum of Understanding (MoU) with any \nnon-governmental body for providing “Digital/ Online Content”. \n \n(b) and (c)  In order to provide the best t eaching-learning resour ces to the students \nacross the country, Government is launc hing Massive Open Online Courses (MOOCs) \nthrough Online Learning Portal named SWAYAM. Through this, it would be possible for \nany student or any school drop-out  to join virtual classes o ffered by the best teachers in \nthe Country, interact with the teacher, take tests, earn academic credits and transfer them \non their academic record. The courses o ffered in this portal will cover 9\nth Class to Post \nGraduation levels. SWAYAM woul d provide one stop web location for interactive e-\ncontent for all courses having facility of peer group interact ion and discussion forums to \nclarify doubts. SWAYAM and a number of MOOCs are likely to be launched soon. \n \nGovernment has launched 'Prashikshak', a teacher education portal on 30th June 2016 for \nbettering the standards of District Institutes  of Education and Tr aining (DIETs) and \nteachers training.   \n \n(d)  The Massive Open Online Courses (M OOCs) offered through SWAYAM will be \ninteractive and prepared by the best teachers in the country. Courses delivered through \nSWAYAM will be available free of cost to the learners,  however students wanting \ncertifications shall be register ed and offered a certificate on successful completion of the \ncourse, with a little fee. At the end of eac h course, there will be an assessment of the \nstudent through proctored examination and the credits secured in this exam could be \ntransferred to the academic record of the students. \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S9_U_109": "1\n \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.109\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25.7.2016\n \nSRAVANA 3, 1938 (SAKA)\n \n \n \nANCIENT WORSHIP PLACES\n \n \n \n+*109.\n \nSHRI  KRUPAL BALAJI TUMANE:\n \nSHRI DEVENDRA SINGH BHOLE:\n \n \nWill the Minister of CULTURE be \npleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nwhether the Government has identified ancient places of worships in the country \nand if so, the location\n-\nwise details of such places in the country;\n \n(b)\n \nwhether the ancient places of worships located in different parts of the  \ncountry \nhave not been covered under the protected list of the Archaeological Survey of \nIndia, if so, the reasons therefor;\n \n(c)\n \nwhether the Government proposes to renovate such ancient sites and temples \nand declared them as places of tourist interest and i\nf so, the details thereof, \nState/UT\n-\nwise; and\n \n(d)\n \nthe details of funds sanctioned and utilized for the renovation and restoration of \nidentified ancient temples and sites in the country, State/UT\n-\nwise? \n \n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE, CULTURE AND TOURISM (I\nNDEPENDENT CHARGE)\n \n \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA)\n \n \n \n(a)to(d)\n \nA Statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n2\n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.109 FOR 25.7.2016\n \n \n(a)\n \nArchaeological Survey of India identifies new places/sites including \nmonuments (religious, non\n-\nreligious and others) through various means \nsuch as village to village survey through its field offices. \n \n \nIn this process in \nthe year 2015\n-\n16 in all \n1820\n \nvillag\nes were surveyed out of which \n822\n \nhave \nrevealed remains of archaeological significance including 386 places of \nworship. \n \nA State\n-\nwise abstract indicating p\nlaces of worship is at \nAnnexure\n–\n \nI. \n \n \n(b)\n \nOur country has \nin\n-\nnumerable number of places of worship a\nll over the \ncountry, out of which \na \nfew of them have been declared protected.  \nArchaeological Survey of India protects only such monuments which meet \nthe criteria specified under Section 2 of Ancient Monuments and \nArchaeological Sites and Remains Act, 1958\n.\n \n \n(c)\n \nIn addition to conservation of protected monuments, Archaeological \nSurvey of India takes up conservation of religious places, not protected by \nArchaeological Survey of India, as a Special work. Most of the religious \nplaces are visited by large numb\ner of devotees, scholars besides \nenthusiast and as such they are places of tourist interest as well.  \nHowever, there is no provision to declare such places as of tourist interest \nunder the Ancient Monuments and Archaeological Sites and Remains Act, \n1958. \n \n \n(d)\n \nThe expenditure incurred on conservation, preservation and restoration of \ncentrally protected monuments (including temples and sites) during the last \nthree years and provisions made for this year is at Annexure \n–\nII.  Further, \nexpenditure incurred on \nconservation, preservation and restoration of non\n-\nprotected monuments/religious places is at Annexure\n-\nIII. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n3\n \n \n \n \nANNEXURE \n–\nI\n \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.109\n \nFOR 25.7.2016\n \n \nSTATEMENT SHOWING PLACES SURVEYED BY THE ARCHAEOLOGICAL \nSURVEY OF INDIA AND NUMBER OF RELIGIOUS PLACES IDENTIFIED DURING \nTHE YEAR 2015\n-\n16 \n \n \nSl.\n \nNo.\n \nState\n \nTotal \nvillages \nsurveyed\n \nNumber of villages \nyielding antiquarian \nremains\n \nNumber of \nreligious places \nidentified \n \n1.\n \nBihar\n \n60\n \n3\n \n00\n \n2.\n \nChhattisgarh\n \n67\n \n10\n \n03\n \n3.\n \nGoa\n \n50\n \n50\n \n12\n \n4.\n \nGujarat\n \n83\n \n54\n \n \n33\n \n5.\n \nHimachal \nPradesh\n \n237\n \n85\n \n61\n \n6.\n \n