    "ls|LS16_S9_U_172": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 172 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.07.2016 \n \nFunctioning of AICTE \n172. SHRI SANJAY DHOTRE: \nSHRI BHARTRUHARI MAHTAB: \nSHRI RAHUL SHEWALE: \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government has conducted any study to measure improvement in \nthe functioning of All India Council for Technical Education (AICTE) since \nimplementation of the recommendations of the Kaw Committee; \n(b) if so, the details and outcome thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; \n(c) the funds allocated and utilised for research and development and improve the \nfunctioning of AICTE in the country during the last three years and the current \nyear, State/UT-wise; and \n(d) whether the Government ha s received complaints of irregularities/ corruption in \nthe functioning of AICTE in the country and \n(e) if so, the details thereof, State/UTwise and the reasons therefor along with the \naction taken/being taken by the Government on such complaints so far? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SH. PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n(a) & (b):   The Government has been monitoring the implementation of the report of the \nAICTE Review Committee which has been submitted in April 2015. Based on these \nrecommendations, the AICTE has been restructured to meet the demands of student \nfraternity and technical institutions by promoting R&D, Vocational Education, Online \nEducation, inclusivity and transparency.  Now, the approval system has become online \nand therefore more efficient and transparent. \n \n(c): The state-wise expenditure for the Research Programs during the last three financial \nyears is at Annexure-I. \n \n(d) & (e):   There have been (9) complaints against officials in AICTE.  These complaints are \nentrusted for examination by a committee head ed by retired Justice of High Court. The \nState-wise list of the complaints against AICTE and action taken thereon is at annexure-II. \n***** \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure as referred to in reply to  Part ( c ) of the Lok Sabha Unstarre\nFunctioning of AICTE\n   2013-14 \nSTATE \n Scheme \nResearch Promotion \nScheme \nResearch Park Quality Improvement \nProgramme \nInnovation Pro\nScheme\nFund \nAllocation  \nExpenditur\ne  \nFund \nAllocatio\nn  \nExpenditur\ne  \nFund \nAllocatio\nn  \nExpenditur\ne  \nFund \nAllocatio\nn  \nExp\nAndhra \nPradesh   24007541   0   2425215\nArunachal \nP r a d e h    0  0  0  \nAssam   7900001   0   0   \nB i h a r    0  0  0  \nChandigarh   0   0   3678842   \nChhatisgarh   4428510   0       \nDelhi   3159844   0 9472436\nGoa  1985824 0   \nGujrat  8430374 0 300000\nHaryana   8772746   0   0   \nHimachal \nPradesh   1633334   0   0   \nJammu & \nKashmir   1243334   0   0   \nJharkhand   582353   0 2448484\nKarnataka   19033630   0   14171941   \nKerala   2140000   0   777000   \nMadhya \nPradesh   6820589   0   0\nMaharashtra   37313047   0   24556150   \n\nM a n i p u r    0  0  0  \nMeghalaya  0 0 0\nM i z o r a m   000\nNagaland  0 0 0\nOdisha   4551667   0   1840887   \nPondicherry   0   0   2314500   \nPunjab   7131804   0   1799000   \nRajasthan   2290001   0   0   \nS k k i m    0  0  0  \nTamilnadu   22029205   0   29376783   \nUttar Pradesh   2012549   0   13116246   \nUttarakhand   0   0   13779633   \nWest Bengal   1667668   0   11508840   \nTotal 500000000 167134021 80000000 0 60000000 131565957 10000000\n \n\nANNEXURE –II \nANNEXURE AS REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (e) OF THE LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 172 FOR REPLY ON 18.07.2016 ASKED BY  SHRI SANJAY \nDHOTRE, SHRI BHARTUHARI MAHTAB AND  SHRI RAHUL SHEWALE REGARDING \nFUNCTIONING OF AICTE \nS.No. State Received from  Details Action Taken  \n1 Delhi Complaint of Bijender \nKumar Passi and Shri \nA.K. Gupta \n Complaint \nagainst AICTE \nofficials \nPlaced before One Man \nJustice (Retd.) \nCommitt