    "ls|LS16_S9_U_177": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES, \nRIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. †* 177 \nANSWERED ON 28.07.2016 \n \nRESTORATION OF WATER BODIES  \n \n†*177.  SHRI SUBHASH CHANDRA BAHERIA \n \nWill the Minister of WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA \nREJUVENATION be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) the number of old water resources revived under the repair, restoration and renovation \nscheme of the Government in view of the shortage of water resources in various States \nparticularly in Rajasthan;  \n(b) the names of the water resources proposed to be repaired/restored in future; and  \n(c) whether a number of Detailed Project Reports (DPRs) are pending for approval under this \nscheme and if so, the time by which such approval is likely to be granted? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA \nREJUVENATION  \n(SUSHRI UMA BHARTI) \n(a) to (c) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nStatement Referred to in Reply of para (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. \n*177 for answer on 28.07.2016 regarding “Restoration of Water Bodies” \n \n(a) Water Resources Project s are planned, funded, executed and maintained by the State \nGovernments themselves as per their own  resources and priority. In order to supplement the \nefforts of the State Governments, Government of India provides technical and financial \nassistance to State Governments to encourage sustainable development and efficient \nmanagement of water resources thro ugh various schemes and programmes such as \nAccelerated Irrigation Benefits Programme (AIBP); and scheme of Repair, Renovation and \nRestoration (RRR) of water bodies etc. \n \nUnder RRR of Water Bodies scheme, a  total of 11865 old water bodies have been revived \nincluding 26 water bodies in the State of Rajasthan. The State -wise details are given at \nAnnexure-I. \n \n(b) & (c) During XII Plan, Proposals for 3739 water bodies have been received from various \nStates for their inclusion under RRR scheme. Out of these, 1354 water bodies for which \nDetailed Project Report (DPR) have been submitted by the concerned State Government as \nper the guidelines of the schemes, have been included for funding under this scheme. State -\nwise details of these water bodies are given at Annexure-II. \n \nIn respect of proposals for  the balance 2385 water bodies, CWC has made certain \nobservations. The compliance for the same has not been received from concerned State \nGovernments. The time taken for approval for inclusion of projects under RRR scheme \ndepends upon the time taken by the concerned State Governments to formulate the proposal \nas per guidelines.   \n \n \n  \n\n                                                                                  Annexure-I  \n \nAnnexure-I referred to in reply to Part  (a) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. *177 for reply \non 28.07.2016 regarding \"Restoration of Water Bodies\".  \n \nNumber of water bodies completed under RRR of Water Bodies scheme since inception \n \nSl \nNo State \nPilot \nscheme  (X \nPlan) \nXI Plan XII Plan \nExternal \nsupport \nDomestic  \n1 Andhra Pradesh 278 854 100  \n2 Bihar  6  14  \n3 Chattishgarh 10  109  \n4 Gujarat 41  28  \n5 Himachal Pradesh 13    \n6 Haryana   3  \n7 Jammu & Kashmir 22    \n8 Jharkhand 60    \n9 Odisha 127 168 1128 38 \n10 Uttar Pradesh   28  \n13 Kartnataka 297 1047 424  \n14 Kerala 21    \n15 Madhya Pradesh 70  78 82 \n16 Maharashtra 32  105  \n17 Meghalaya   1  \n18 Tamil Nadu 44 5009   \n19 Rajasthan 5  16 5 \n20 Manipur     \n21 Telangana  976 567  \n22 West Bengal  60    \nTotal 1085 8054 2601 125 \n \n \n    \n \n\n                                                                                                                                                    Annexure-II \n \nAnnexure-II referred to in reply to Part “b & c” of 