    "ls|LS16_S9_U_214": "LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 214 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 1ST AUGUST, 2016 \n \nUNIFORM PRICES OF PETROL/DIESEL \n \n*214.  SHRI S. SELVAKUMARA CHINNAYAN:  \n SHRI MALLIKARJUN KHARGE: \n \nisVªksfy;e vkSj izkÑfrd xSl ea=h \n \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the factors taken into account and mechanism to determine price of petroleum products;  \n \n(b) whether the Government has any proposal to fix uniform prices of petrol and diesel across \nthe country and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) the time by which the said proposal is likely to be implemented; and  \n \n(d) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nisVªksfy;e vkSj izkÑfrd xSl ea=h (Lora= izHkkj) \n¼Jh /keZsUnz iz/kku½ \nMINISTER OF STATE (I/C) IN THE MINISTRY OF PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN)   \n(a) to (d): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n\nStatement referred to in reply to parts (a) to (d) of the Lok Sabha Starred Question No. \n214 asked by Shri S. Selvak umara Chinnayan and Shri Mallikarjun Kharge to be \nanswered on 1st August, 2016 regarding “Uniform Prices of Petrol/Diesel”. \n \n(a): The prices of Petrol and Diesel have been made market determined by the \nGovernment effective 26 th June, 2010 and 19 th October, 2014 respectively.   Since then, the \nPublic Sector Oil Marketing Companies (OMCs) take appropriate decision on pricing of \nPetrol and Diesel in line with their international prices and other market conditions. The \nGovernment continues to modulate the effective price to consumer for Subsidized Domestic \nLPG and Retail Selling Price (RSP) of PDS Kerosene.   Public Sector OMCs are at present \napplying Trade Parity Pricing methodology to compute the Retail Selling Price (RSP) of \nPetrol and Diesel.  Import  Parity Price (IPP) is applied for pricing of PDS Kerosene and \nDomestic LPG. \n \n(b) to ( d): The basic prices of Petrol and Diesel are uniform across the country. However, \nthe final selling prices vary from state to state/ market to market due to changes in other \nelements such as freight, delivery charges, Sales tax/VAT, local levies etc.  \n \nx-x-x-x-x-x \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S9_U_215": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM  \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*215  \nANSWERED ON 01.08.2016  \n \nMAINTENANCE OF TOURIST SPOTS  \n \n*215. SHRI R. GOPALAKRISHNAN:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Government has instituted  any structured \nmechanism to maintain tourist spots in different States of \nthe country and if so, the details thereof;  \n(b)  whether the Government has launched any specific \nscheme in this regard;  \n(c)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons th erefor; \nand  \n(d)  the year/State -wise and tourist place -wise details of the \nfunds allocated and utilised for this purpose during the \nlast two years and the current year?  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA)  \n \n(a)  to (d):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n \n********* \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION \nNO.*215 ANSWERED ON 01.08.2016 REGARDING MAINTENANCE OF \nTOURIST SPOTS. \n \n(a) to (d): The Ministry of Tourism (MoT) under its Plan Schemes  \nSwadesh Darshan and National Mission on Pilgrimage Rejuvenation \nand Spiritual Augmentation Drive (PRASAD) provides Central \nFinancial Assistance (CFA) to State Governments/Union Territory \nAdministrations for the development of tourism \ndestinations/sites/spots, subject to the availability of funds, \nliquidation of pending utilization certificates against the funds \nreleased earlier and adherence to the relevant scheme guidelines. \nMaintenance of assets created under these Schemes is the \nresponsibility of the concerned State/UTs. \n \n MoT also provides funds to the Central Agencies for certain \ninfrastructural development in places of tourist interest, such as \nillumination, sound & light shows, development of cruise terminals \netc. under the Plan Scheme “Assistance to  Central Agencies for \nTourism Infrastructure Development”. The Revised Guidelines dated \n24.09.2015 of this scheme provide for Operation & Maintenance \nCost for initial period of 3 years from the date of start of operation, \nsubject to certain conditions and limits. \n \n The Archaeological Survey of India (ASI) has 3686 numbers of \nprotected monuments of National importance for which there is a \nstructured mechanism fo r conservation and maintenance. The \nconservation work on them is attended regularly by the ASI und er \nthe allocation of budget for \"Conservation of Ancient Monuments\". \nThe details of funds allocated and expenditure incurred for last two \nyears and allocation for the current financial year, State -wise, are \ngiven in Annexure. \n \n***************\n\nANNEXURE \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. *215 ANSWERED ON 01.08.2016 REGARDING \nMAINTENANCE OF TOURIST SPOTS. \n \nSTATE/UT-WISE DETAILS OF FUNDS ALLOCATED AND UTILISED FOR \nCONSERVATION OF PROTECTED MONUMENTS UNDER ASI FOR THE LAST \nTWO YEARS AND ALLOCATION FOR CURRENT FINANCIAL YEAR \n \n(Rs. in lakhs) \nSl. \nNo. \nName of \nState/UT \nNumber of \nprotected \nmonuments \nCircle / \nBranch \nAllocation/Expenditure  \n2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 \n(Allocation) \n1. Uttar \nPradesh \n743 Agra Circle 1404.99 1270.00 1060.00 \nLucknow \nCircle \n1165.00 945.08 925.00 \nSarnath \nCircle \n534.99 495.00 500.00 \n2. Maharashtra  285 Aurangabad \nCircle \n695.00 629.05 500.00 \nMumbai \nCircle \n645.00 902.82 725.00 \nNagpur \nCircle \n444.98 845.00 610.00 \n3. Karnataka 506 Bangalore \nCircle \n1515.99 1427.02 1125.00 \nMini Circle \nHampi \n90.00 401.24 575.00 \nDharwad \nCircle \n713.94 716.42 675.00 \n4. Madhya \nPradesh \n292 Bhopal Circle  956.99 1261.01 925.00 \n5. Odisha 79 Bhubaneswar \nCircle \n596.99 679.52 605.00 \n6. West Bengal  136 Kolkata \nCircle \n549.63 537.95 550.00 \nSikkim 03  \n7. Tamil Nadu,  413 Chennai \nCircle \n1070.01 919.10 775.00 \nPuducherry \n(UT) \n07  \n8. Punjab 33 Chandig