    "ls|LS16_S9_U_238": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES AND PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \nDEPARTMENT OF PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No.238 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.7.2016 \n \nSurplus Land with CPSES \n \n \n238.  SHRIMATI  RAKSHATAI  KHADSE: \n \n \nWill the Minister of HEAVY INDUSTRIES & PUBLIC ENTERPRISES be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has any proposal for collaboration and pooling resources of CPSEs \nsuch as financial, technical and manpower to enable better   and more optimal solu tions in \nincreasing customer driven market; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the Government is taking steps to identify and unlock the surplus land available \nwith CPSEs as it can be used in generating the much needed public investments to boost the \neconomy and increase employment opportunities; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \n  THE MINISTER OF STATE FOR HEAVY INDUSTRIES & PUBLIC ENTERPRISES  \n(SHRI BABUL SUPRIYO) \n \n(a) & (b): Central Public Sector Enterprises (CPSEs) operate in a competitive environment \nand they collaborate and pool resources to respond to the changing market situations. Policy \nformulation and strategic responsiveness is a continuous and dynamic exercise and is taken to \nmeet emerging challenges. Department of Public Enterprises has not received any proposal for \ncollaboration and pooling of resources of CPSEs. \n \n(c) & (d): A web portal has been set up by the Ministry of Urban Development to develop a \ncentralized database of inventory o f all Government land including that belonging to \nGovernment controlled Statutory Authorities and CPSEs. This centralized database will help in \nthe optimum utilization of land with the CPSEs. \n* * * ",
    "ls|LS16_S9_U_239": " \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES AND PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \nDEPARTMENT OF HEAVY INDUSTRY \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.239 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 19.07.2016 \n  \n \nBan on Diesel Vehicle \n \n239. SHRI P. NAGARAJAN: \n \n Will the Minister of HEAVY INDUSTRIES AND PUBLIC ENTERPRISES be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware of the ban on vehicles using diesel fuel in the country;  \n(b) if so, whether any studies has been conducted on the impact of such ban on the automobile \nindustries in the country; and  \n(c) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF  STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF  HEAVY INDUSTRIES AND PUBLIC \nENTERPRISES (SHRI BABUL SUPRIYO) \n \n(a): No, Madam. \nHowever, the Hon’ble Supreme Court in the matter of M.C.Mehta vs. UOI & Ors has ordered \nfor ban on registration of diesel vehicles with capacity more than 2000 cc on 16 th December \n2016 in the NCR of Delhi till 31 st March 2016, whi ch was subsequently extended till 30 th \nApril 2016. The ban has further been extended till the hearing of matter. \n \n(b):  No, Madam.  \n \n(c):  Does not arise in view of (b) above. \n \n******* ",
    "ls|LS16_S9_U_24": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(DEPARTMENT OF COMMERCE) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 24 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18TH JULY, 2016 \n \nTEA EXPORTS \n24.  SHRIMATI VANAROJA R.: \nWill the Minister of COMMERCE & INDUSTRY  (वािणÏय एवं उɮयोग मंत्री ) be \npleased to state: \n(a) whether it is true that the countries which have helped in boos ting tea exports from \nIndia and which face intense competition from Kenya and Sri Lan ka, are Russia, \nIran and Pakistan and if so, the details thereof;  \n(b) whether some key markets have been identified by the Government  for \nspearheading India's tea export and if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether the export prices have been signed keeping in view the trend of declining \ntea prices and lower average realisation; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nokf.kT; ,oa m|ksx jkT; ea=h ¼Jherh fueZyk lhrkje.k½ ¼Lora= izHkkj½ \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY \n(INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n(SMT. NIRMALA SITHARAMAN) \n \n(a) to (d):  Yes, Madam.  Increase of tea exports from India were registered primarily in  Russia, \nIran and Pakistan along with other countries as per details in the following Table. \nSl. \nNo.  Country \n2015‐16  2014‐2015  Growth (%) \nQuantity \n(M. Kgs) \nValue  \n(Rs. Crs.) \nQty \n(M.Kgs.) \nValue \n(Rs. Crs) \nQty \n (M. Kgs.) \nValue  \n(Rs. Crs) \n1  Iran  22.13  571.81 18.14 478.51 22  19.5\n2  Russia  48.23  670.57 39.4 582.28 22.41  15.16\n3  Pakistan  19.37  192.61 15.2 125.12 27.43  53.94\n \n\nThe five markets viz. Russia, Kaza khstan, USA, Iran and Egypt have been identified as potential \nmarkets  for  increasing  Indian  exports  based  on  the  parameters  o f  their  “Market \nattractiveness” and “Ability to serve”. In addition, China and  Chile have also been added for \nsustained promotion.Decline in export price realizations for te a during 2015‐16 as compared \nto  2014‐15  is  attributed  to  the  factors  of  global  over‐supply  s ituation  and  currency \nfluctuations (sharp devaluation) in some key markets like Russi a, Kazakhstan, Egypt leading to \npurchase of cheaper teas.  \n****** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S9_U_240": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*240 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 2ND AUGUST, 2016/SHRAVANA 11, 1938 (SAKA) \n \nISIS LINKS WITH MISSING PERSONS \n \n*240.  SHRI M.B. RAJESH: \nSHRI N.K. PREMACHANDRAN: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has confirmed the ISIS links of a number of \npersons gone missing from various parts of the country including Kerala \nrecently; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the reaction of the Government thereto; \n \n(c) whether the Government has tracked IS sleeper cells in the country; \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(e) the mechanism to track and counter online radicalisation of youth by \nvarious religious extremist organizations including ISIS? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n (SHRI RAJNATH SINGH) \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n****** \n \n \n \n \n \n\n-2- \n \nSTATEMENT REF ERRED TO IN REPLY TO THE LO K SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.*240 FOR 02.08.2016. \n \n(a) & (b): Some persons have been reported missing from some parts of \nKerala, who are suspected to have joined terrorist outfits like ISIS, but \ntheir links with ISIS is not yet been established.  Kerala Police has \nregistered 9 cases in this connection. \n \n(c) & (d): The National Investigation Agency (NIA), Maharashtra Police, \nKarnataka Police, Madhya Pradesh Police, Telangana Police and Tamil \nNadu Police  have registered cases to investigate the alleged links of \nIndian youth with ISIS/ISIL/IS and have so far arrested 54 persons.   \n \n(e) : The terrorist outfit, ISIS, is using various platforms to propagate its \nideology and to attract recruits from across the  world.  The Intelligence \nand Security Agencies maintain a close watch to identify potential \nrecruits.   Various programmes are being undertaken by the Central and \nState Governments to deal with the issue of counter radicalization and \nde-radicalization.   \n \n******* ",
    "ls|LS16_S9_U_241": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CHEMICALS & FERTILIZERS \nDEPARTMENT OF FERTILIZERS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 241 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON :19.07.2016 \n \n \nSupply of DAP fertilizers  \n \n \n241 SHRI BHAIRON PRASAD MISHRA: \n  \n \n Will the Minister of CHEMICALS & FERTILIZERS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has taken any measures to ensure sufficient supply  of DAP \nfertilizers in the country; and   \n \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof?  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE   MINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS, SHIPPING, \nROAD TRANSPORT & HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI  MANSUKH  L. MANDAVIYA) \n(a)& (b):  Yes Madam, Government has taken following measures to ensure sufficient supply of \nDAP fertilizers in the country.  The month -wise demand of subsidized fertilizers inc luding DAP \nwas assessed and projected by the Department of Agriculture & Co- operation and Farmers \nWelfare (DAC&FW) in consultation with the State Governments before commencement of each \ncropping season.  \n(ii)  On the basis of month- wise & state -wise projec tion given by DAC&FW, Department of \nFertilizers is allocating sufficient/ adequate quantities of fertilizers to States by issuing monthly \nsupply plan and continuously monitoring the availability through following system: \n(iii)   The movement of all major subsidized fertilizers is being monitored throughout the country \nby an on- line web based monitoring system ( www.urvarak.co.in) also called as Fertilizer \nMonitoring System (FMS); \n \n\n: 2 : \n(iv):  The State Governments are regularly advised to coordinate with manufacturers and \nimporters of fertilizers for streamlining the supplies through timely placement of indents for \nrailway rakes through their state institutional agencies like Markfed etc. \n(v):  Regular Weekly Video Conference is conducted jointly by Department of Agriculture, \nCooperation & Farmers Welfare (DAC&FW), Department of Fertilizers (DoF), and Ministry of \nRailways with State Agriculture Officials and corrective actions are taken to di spatch fertilizer as \nindicated by the State Governments. \n  \n It is also stated that in the last year the availability of DAP was 101.28 LMT against the \nsales of 97.47 LMT and in the current year upto June, 2016, the availability of DAP is 25.06 \nLMT against the sales of 15.07 LMT and there is no shortage. \n \n********* \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S9_U_242": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.242 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 19THJULY, 2016/ASHADHA 28, 1938 (SAKA) \n \nCRIME BY JUVENILES \n \n242.  DR. K. GOPAL: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether it is true that sexual offences  by juveniles are on the rise in \nmany parts of the country; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government has  directed the State Governments to \nenhance the police density in areas where such  crimes are reported  \nfrequently; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI HANSRAJ GANGARAM AHIR) \n \n(a) to (b):    The increase in number of crimes reported are attributed to \nseveral measures taken by the Union Government along with State \nGovernments / Union Territory Administrations due to truthful reporting of \ncrime and mandatory registration of FIRs for various cr imes / offences \ncommitted. The State/UT wise total number of cases reported against \njuveniles during the year 2012-2014 is at Annexure. \n….2/ \n \n\n-2- \nL.S.US.Q.NO.242 FOR 19.07.2016 \n \n(c) to (d): The Ministry of Home Affair s issue s various Advisories \nregarding m atter of urgent importance from time to time  which are  \navailable on the website of the Ministry of Home Affairs viz  \nhttp://mha.nic.in.  Further, Police’ and ‘Public Order’ being State subjects, \naction with respect to maintenance of law and order lies primarily in the \ndomain of the State Governments . The issue of crime by juveniles is \nmainly dealt through Juvenile Justice (Care and Protection of Children) \nAct 2000 which provides for reformative care in case of   children/juvenile  \nin conflict with law. The Ministry of Women and Child Development is \nimplementing a Centrally Sponsored Scheme, namely, Integrated Child \nProtection Scheme (ICPS) for rehabilitation and reintegration of children in \ndifficult circumstances.   \n \n            ******\n\n          \n                                  Page 1 of 1 of Annexure \n                  L.S.US.Q.NO.242 FOR 19.07.2016  \nState/UT wise juveniles in conflict with law under various sexual crimes under IPC during 2012-2014 \n \nS.No. State/UT \n2012 2013     2014 \nRape Assault on \nwomen with \nintent to \noutrage her \nModesty \nInsult to \nthe \nModesty \nof Women \nTotal \nSexual \nCrimes \nRape Assault on \nwomen with \nintent to \noutrage her \nModesty \nInsult to \nthe \nModesty of \nWomen \nTotal \nSexual \nCrimes \nRape Attempt to \ncommit Rape* \nAssault on \nwomen with \nintent to \noutrage her \nModesty \nInsult to \nthe \nModesty \nof Women \nTotal Sexual \nCrimes \n1 Andhra Pradesh 70 39 62 171 98 105 117 320 40 6 33 20 99 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 1 5 0 6 0 0 0 0 11 0 4 0 15 \n3 Assam 56 12 0 68 49 5 0 54 58 1 7 0 66 \n4 Bihar 26 14 2 42 66 33 1 100 43 27 18 11 99 \n5 Chhattisgarh 0 60 6 66 122 112 7 241 105 2 87 1 195 \n6 Goa 2 2 0 4 1 1 0 2 4 1 1 0 6 \n7 Gujarat 20 24 0 44 24 41 2 67 36 0 35 2 73 \n8 Haryana 41 14 6 61 50 56 12 118 65 5 65 0 135 \n9 Himachal Pradesh 10 4 0 14 13 6 1 20 10 0 10 0 20 \n10 Jammu & Kashmir 2 3 0 5 3 4 3 10 4 0 4 0 8 \n11 Jharkhand 22 1 0 23 32 0 0 32 22 0 1 0 23 \n12 Karnataka 12 2 0 14 17 5 1 23 26 0 8 0 34 \n13 Kerala 25 5 4 34 32 16 5 53 39 0 17 0 56 \n14 Madhya Pradesh 249 217 49 515 347 359 58 764 434 3 425 14 876 \n15 Maharashtra 89 96 40 225 197 312 76 585 208 0 328 28 564 \n16 Manipur 0 0 0 0 1 0 0 1 7 0 0 0 7 \n17 Meghalaya 25 2 0 27 23 1 0 24 11 0 1 1 13 \n18 Mizoram 21 1 0 22 8 3 0 11 15 0 0 0 15 \n19 Nagaland 2 0 0 2 0 0 0 0 2 0 2 0 4 \n20 Odisha 70 15 0 85 91 34 2 127 79 0 37 4 120 \n21 Punjab 14 0 0 14 12 17 0 29 44 6 8 0 58 \n22 Rajasthan 102 39 1 142 183 101 1 285 149 6 101 1 257 \n23 Sikkim 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 3 0 2 0 5 \n24 Tamil Nadu 27 11 0 38 32 7 2 41 12 0 1 4 17 \n25 Telangana                 63 0 29 15 107 \n26 Tripura 23 1 0 24 8 3 0 1